From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:17:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: ane-isp: build the link only where the
 ANE driver provides it

The ISP's ML noise reduction asks the ANE driver for an endpoint through
include/linux/soc/apple/ane-isp.h. The header declares the real calls
whenever the ANE driver is reachable, but no ANE driver implements them
yet, so a kernel with both drivers as modules fails to link apple-isp.

Gate the declarations on a new DRM_ACCEL_ANE_ISP_LINK option, off by
default, for the ANE driver to select once it provides the interface.
Until then the ISP driver uses the stubs, which report no link, and the
camera works as before.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/accel/ane/Kconfig         | 11 +++++++++++
 include/linux/soc/apple/ane-isp.h |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/ane/Kconfig b/drivers/accel/ane/Kconfig
index 6b40340d69..8746b9f029 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/ane/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/accel/ane/Kconfig
@@ -33,6 +33,17 @@ config DRM_ACCEL_ANE
 	  the M1 family will be called ane, and the module for the M2 family
 	  will be called ane_t6021.
 
+config DRM_ACCEL_ANE_ISP_LINK
+	bool "Apple Neural Engine link for the camera ISP"
+	depends on DRM_ACCEL_ANE
+	default n
+	help
+	  The camera ISP runs some of its algorithms on the Neural Engine
+	  and needs the ANE driver to set up an endpoint for it
+	  (include/linux/soc/apple/ane-isp.h). Say Y only once the ANE
+	  driver provides that interface; until then the ISP driver uses
+	  the stubs and works without the Neural Engine.
+
 config DRM_ACCEL_ANE_KUNIT_TEST
 	tristate "KUnit tests for the Apple Neural Engine driver" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
 	depends on DRM_ACCEL_ANE && KUNIT
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/ane-isp.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/ane-isp.h
index 0a4430771a..ac177395a2 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/ane-isp.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/ane-isp.h
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ struct ane_isp_endpoint {
 	u32 ane_doorbell_sel;
 };
 
-#if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_DRM_ACCEL_ANE)
+#if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_DRM_ACCEL_ANE) && IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DRM_ACCEL_ANE_ISP_LINK)
 struct ane_isp_link *ane_isp_link_get(struct device *isp_dev, struct device_node *ane_np);
 void ane_isp_link_put(struct ane_isp_link *link);
 int ane_isp_endpoint_enable(struct ane_isp_link *link, const char *afpp,
-- 
